# the PE/COFF writer, the PE/COFF model into bytes
#
# the extents of the model tile the file, so each is placed in order through
# the layout plan, the plan is sealed, and each is written at the offset the
# plan recorded. the model holds every header number as written, so before a
# byte is written the numbers that place an extent are checked against the
# plan: the PE signature against the DOS header's pointer, the optional
# header and section table against the file header, each section's bytes,
# relocations and line numbers against its header, the symbol and string
# tables against the file header, and every count against the table it
# counts. a model that disagrees with its own extents is refused, never
# written. a bigobj's signature words and class id are written from the table
# rows the reader checks them against. an image whose section alignment is
# below its file alignment is refused, and an image checksum the reader found
# to be the specification's checksum is computed over the bytes written.
# the addresses data directories and typed pieces hold are written as held.

